#!/usr/bin/env python3
# 12 October 2026: task MI, bass stem iteration. Fits per note a release time, a low-pass tilt (dB per octave above a
# corner), an attack gain and a sustain level against the reference bass stem, in MusicCritic's third-octave domain
# (zrmd/audio/stems/bass.py), then alternates with a re-measure of the stem's residual bed and per-bar equaliser
# (resynth.measure_residual / measure_eq, the same calls as ResynthMusic.fit_stem_fx). Every candidate is a new
# folder stem-iter/bass/V_NNN (never overwritten) with bass.wav, params.json and scores.json (MusicCritic diagnosis
# plus resynth's stable scores: tfBands, plossEvents, plossBarNoOnset).
#   IterateBass.py selftest            both ways: neutral fit = V_034 bit for bit (green); a sabotaged tilt drops the
#                                      critic by >= 3 (red); band model E agrees with the critic within 0.05
#   IterateBass.py run [--base V_034] [--max 12]
#   IterateBass.py mix --version V_NNN the full mix of the base with this bass stem (mix bus replayed), scored
# FR : iteration de la piste basse, ajustement par note puis re-mesure de l'egaliseur, une version par essai.
